  "behavior": [
    "One byte-span writer recovers ostream/C stderr errors before output and after failure, preserving stream exception masks and renderer exception identity.",
    "Ordinary diagnostic writes remain best-effort; preserved-file notices require successful insertion and explicit flushing. Failed notices remain owned for restoration.",
    "A function-pointer-backed default sink lives in aligned static storage without heap allocation or a registered destructor, including first use and late static shutdown.",
    "Native curses startup uses checked newterm and owns SCREEN through endwin/delscreen. Shared ownership headers expose no curses macros.",
    "Snapshot/restoration responsibility begins before a potentially mutating operation, not during member construction. Validation errors leave background terminals untouched.",
    "Private terminal handles reject duplicate acquisition and use after close; checked active-mode changes go through the adapter; close remains idempotent and allocation-free.",
    "ASCII is handled before the shared UTF-8 decoder. Canonical repair grouping and the approved selective Unicode path policy are unchanged.",
    "Live, cleanup, and file replay ordering, worker quiescence, independent drains, full paths, and best-effort emergency delivery are retained."
  ],
